t_operation_details', arguments={'platform': 'PowerPoint', 'operation': 'CreatePresentation'}, thought='Let me get the details for creating PowerPoint presentations:', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"# Creating PowerPoint Presentations with python-pptx\\\\n\\\\n## Overview\\\\nThis SOP outlines the process for creating professional PowerPoint presentations programmatically using the python-pptx library.\\\\n\\\\n## Prerequisites\\\\n- Python 3.x installed\\\\n- python-pptx library installed (`pip install python-pptx`)\\\\n\\\\n## Steps\\\\n\\\\n### 1. Import Required Modules\\\\n```python\\\\nfrom pptx import Presentation\\\\nfrom pptx.util import Inches, Pt\\\\nfrom pptx.enum.text import PP_ALIGN\\\\nfrom pptx.dml.color import RGBColor\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### 2. Create Presentation Object\\\\n```python\\\\nprs = Presentation()\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### 3. Add Slides\\\\n- Use different slide layouts:\\\\n  - `prs.slide_layouts[0]` - Title slide\\\\n  - `prs.slide_layouts[1]` - Title and content\\\\n  - `prs.slide_layouts[5]` - Blank slide\\\\n\\\\n### 4. Add Content to Slides\\\\n- Access title: `slide.shapes.title`\\\\n- Access content: `slide.placeholders[1]`\\\\n- Set text: `shape.text = \\\\\"Your text here\\\\\"`\\\\n\\\\n### 5. Format Content\\\\n- Use bullet points with \\\\\"\\\\u2022\\\\\" character\\\\n- Structure content with clear headings and subpoints\\\\n- Maintain consistent formatting across slides\\\\n\\\\n### 6. Save Presentation\\\\n```python\\\\nprs.save(\\'/path/to/your/presentation.pptx\\')\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## Best Practices\\\\n- Keep slides focused and concise\\\\n- Use consistent formatting and styling\\\\n- Include clear headings and bullet points\\\\n- Test the presentation before finalizing\\\\n- Consider adding visual elements for better engagement\\\\n\\\\n## Example Use Cases\\\\n- Business proposals\\\\n- Technical presentations\\\\n- Research summaries\\\\n- Project updates\\\\n- Training materials\\\\n\\\\n## Troubleshooting\\\\n- Ensure file path is writable\\\\n- Check python-pptx version compatibility\\\\n- Verify slide layout indices are correct\\\\n- Test presentation opening in PowerPoint\\\\n\\\\nThis SOP was successfully used to create a 7-slide presentation about integrating Sotopia into Openhands with clear structure and professional formatting.\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='get_operation_details', arguments={'platform': 'PowerPoint', 'operation': 'CreatePresentation'}), FileReadAction(path='/workspace', start=0, end=-1, thought=\"Now let me check the TAC overview file to understand the company's mission and products:\", action=<ActionType.READ: 'read'>, security_risk=None, impl_source='oh_aci', view_range=None), FileReadObservation(content=\"Here's the files and directories up to 2 levels deep in /workspace, excluding hidden items:\\n/workspace/\", path='/workspace', observation=<ObservationType.READ: 'read'>, impl_source='oh_aci'), CmdRunAction(command='find / -name \"TAC_overview.md\" 2>/dev/null', is_input=False, thought='Let me search for the TAC overview file:', blocking=False, is_static=False, cwd=None, hidden=False, action=<ActionType.RUN: 'run'>, confirmation_state='confirmed', security_risk=None), CmdOutputObservation(content='', command='find / -name \"TAC_overview.md\" 2>/dev/null', observation=<ObservationType.RUN: 'run'>, metadata=CmdOutputMetadata(exit_code=1, pid=-1, username='root', hostname='ecs-d984', working_dir='/outputs', py_interpreter_path='/openhands/poetry/openhands-ai-5O4_aCHf-py3.12/bin/python', prefix='', suffix='\\n[The command completed with exit code 1.]'), hidden=False), CmdRunAction(command='find /workspace -name \"*TAC*\" -o -name \"*overview*\" 2>/dev/null', is_input=False, thought=\"Let me check if there's a TAC overview file in the current directory or search more broa